{
  "sn21.1:0.1": "Linked Discourses 21.1 ",
  "sn21.1:0.2": "1. Monks ",
  "sn21.1:0.3": "With Kolita ",
  "sn21.1:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn21.1:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn21.1:1.3": "There Venerable Mahāmoggallāna addressed the mendicants: ",
  "sn21.1:1.4": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "sn21.1:1.5": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "sn21.1:2.1": "Venerable Mahāmoggallāna said this: ",
  "sn21.1:2.2": "“Just now, reverends, as I was in private retreat this thought came to mind: ",
  "sn21.1:2.3": "‘They speak of this thing called “noble silence”. ",
  "sn21.1:2.4": "What then is this noble silence?’ ",
  "sn21.1:2.5": "It occurred to me: ",
  "sn21.1:2.6": "‘As the placing of the mind and keeping it connected are stilled, a mendicant enters and remains in the second absorption, which has the rapture and bliss born of immersion, with internal clarity and mind at one, without placing the mind and keeping it connected. ",
  "sn21.1:2.7": "This is called noble silence.’ ",
  "sn21.1:2.8": "And so, as the placing of the mind and keeping it connected were stilled, I was entering and remaining in the second absorption, which has the rapture and bliss born of immersion, with internal clarity and mind at one, without placing the mind and keeping it connected. ",
  "sn21.1:2.9": "While I was in that meditation, perception and focus accompanied by placing the mind beset me. ",
  "sn21.1:3.1": "Th